        <p class="about-p">
            I am a Software Engineer from Imperial, Nebraska. After graduating with honors and the highest distinction
            from the University of Nebraska-Lincoln (UNL) in August 2023, I earned my bachelor's degree in computer
            science and a minor in mathematics. My radiant passion for programming fuels my professional choices and
            guides my educational journey.
            <br /><br />
            I fell in love with programming back in my elementary school days. Prompted by my curiosity about video game
            creation and website development, I dived into online courses on Codecademy. This early interest in web and
            game development stayed with me through junior high and high school, increasing in depth when I started
            studying at UNL. My time here was marked by a profound exploration into the intricate aspects of programming
            beyond the basics.
            <br /><br />
            My skills in programming were further sharpened thanks to my diverse experiences in academic coursework,
            personal projects, and an internship at FarmAfield. I've also gained invaluable experience in game
            development and graphic design through my courses and extracurricular activities at different institutes
            like UNL, Reykjavik University (RU), and Chase County High School (CCHS).
            <br /><br />
            Being an attentive, organized, and forward-thinking individual, I consistently deliver top-notch results. My
            natural curiosity and discipline keep me motivated, encouraging steady progress and effectively preventing
            burnout. My ability to work effectively in a team environment further enhances my potential contribution to
            prospective collaborations.
            <br /><br />
            Currently, I work as a Software Developer at Sandhills Global in Lincoln, Nebraska where I develop and
            maintain a web agreement editor. I also maintain various exisiting internal and external facing Web apps
            and APIs.
        </p>
